# Email transport providers

Transactional and marketing email go through a **provider registry**. Built-in transports ship as external plugins (`@bermooda/plugin-resend`, `@bermooda/plugin-sendgrid`, `@bermooda/plugin-aws-ses`). Only one email provider plugin can be active at a time — activate it under **Admin → Plugins**.

Relevant modules: [app/libs/email/index.server.js](mdc:app/libs/email/index.server.js), [app/libs/email-types.server.js](mdc:app/libs/email-types.server.js), plugin sources in sibling repos (`../plugin-resend`, `../plugin-sendgrid`, `../plugin-aws-ses`), templates in [app/emails/index.server.jsx](mdc:app/emails/index.server.jsx).

## What to call

| Use case | Import | Notes |
| ----- | --- | ----- |
| Send a named template | `sendWelcomeEmail`, `sendOrderConfirmationEmail`, … from `#/emails/index.server` | Renders React Email → HTML, then active provider |
| Raw HTML send | `sendEmail` from `#/libs/email/index.server` | Low-level; requires an active email plugin |
| Custom / plugin provider | `defineProvider('email', { name, send })` | Enable under Admin → Plugins (exclusive with other email plugins) |

Do **not** import ESP SDKs from app code outside email provider plugins.

## Configuration

From [`.env.example`](mdc:.env.example):

- `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` — also used to encrypt plugin password settings at rest

Activate one plugin in **Admin → Plugins → Email providers** and enter API keys in that plugin's settings form (encrypted in the `Setting` table). `bermooda install` enables `@bermooda/plugin-resend` by default. Contributors install plugins via `npm run extensions:install`.

## Custom providers (plugins)

```js
import { definePlugin, defineProvider } from '#/core/plugins/index.server';

export const pluginManifest = definePlugin({
  providers: {
    postmark: defineProvider('email', {
      name: 'Postmark',
      async send({ from, to, subject, html, text }) {
        return { success: true };
      },
    }),
  },
});
```

Enabling your plugin deactivates any other email provider plugin automatically.
